WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.330
Bare rock.

2
00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.130
No soil at all.

3
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.510
Yet low mosses can live on it.

4
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.990
Now a pond: open water.

5
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.790
No soil there either.

6
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.110
Leave both alone.

7
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.010
The plants keep changing.

8
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.870
After centuries, in
most of lowland Britain,

9
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.110
both end up as woodland dominated by oak.

10
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.450
So why do such different
starts end so alike?

11
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.070
Is the soil the same?

12
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.890
Do people plant the trees?

13
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.550
In this mission, you'll see
how each step builds soil,

14
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.850
holds water and casts shade,
so new plants can win.

15
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.950
Then you'll explore the oak woodland:
its brown earth soil and its wildlife.

16
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.110
Your mission: explain why bare rock and
a pond both become similar woodland in

17
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.170
lowland Britain.
